Kernir patch 0019: the xar reader counts the headers it returns against the entry limit, not its bare folders

Upstream: libarchive 3.8.10, libarchive/archive_read.c (__archive_read_kernir_names_allowance, from 0016),
archive_read_support_format_xar.c (struct xar, xar_read_header, file_new, xml_end), include/kernir_names.h (its
comment, with 0016's comment in the xar reader). Applies on top of 0001-0018
(0016 and 0018 lines included).

Patch 0016 counted every <file> element against the entry limit, bare folders included: a directory <file> with
only a name and a type, which xar_read_header frees without returning it. Kernir counts the headers it reads, so
a xar of N files and B bare folders was refused once N + B passed the limit, though Kernir would list it whole up
to N = the limit.

The <file> elements xar_read_header returns (kernir_xar_listed, now also its skip test) are counted at </file>, once
their has flags and type are known, and refused over max_entries with 0016's message ("xar archive has more
entries than the entry limit"), the same count Kernir's caller refuses. Every <file> is still allocated when it
opens, so file_new still holds all of them, bare folders included, to a hard limit before calloc: 2 × max_entries
(saturated at UINT64_MAX), the same message. 0016's names total, which grows with every <file> so far, grows with
at most max_entries of them (__archive_read_kernir_names_allowance caps its count, as Kernir's allowances do), so
bare folders past the limit add no name bytes. Archives within 0016's limits read as before.

Apply from Sources/CLibArchive: patch -p1 < patches/0019-xar-bare-folders-entry-cap.patch

